# Public keys allowed to log in to sophon over SSH as james.
#
# Source-only: .chezmoiignore keeps it out of the home directory, and script 11
# copies it to C:\ProgramData\ssh\administrators_authorized_keys. sshd reads
# that file, not ~/.ssh/authorized_keys, for any account in the Administrators
# group, and james is one.
#
# PUBLIC KEYS ONLY. This repo is public. The private half stays on the machine
# that generated it and is never committed anywhere.
#
# One key per line, with these options in front of it:
#
#   restrict   no port, agent or X11 forwarding, no pty.
#   pty        gives back the pty, so `ssh sophon` works by hand.
#
# Generate each key on its client WITH a passphrase. Follow "Authorize a Mac"
# in the README: its commands refuse to make a key without one, and check the
# result. The passphrase is what makes a copied key file useless. No from= address
# restriction: the firewall already limits logins to the LAN, and from= would
# lock a client out whenever its address changed.
#
# Add a line of this form below:
#
#   restrict,pty ssh-ed25519 AAAA... james@neuromancer to sophon
#
# The options must be exactly `restrict` or `restrict,pty`. Script 11 leaves
# any other line out of the server's copy and fails the apply to name it, and
# warns while this file has no key line in it.
